<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Prompt xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <masterLabel>Activity Tab</masterLabel>
    <promptVersions>
        <body>&lt;p&gt;This walkthrough shows how to use the &lt;strong&gt;Activity&lt;/strong&gt; tab to track customer engagements, tasks, calls, and other key activities related to your sales opportunities. Click &lt;strong&gt;Next&lt;/strong&gt; to continue. You can dismiss this walkthrough at any time.&lt;/p&gt;</body>
        <customApplication>standard__LightningSales</customApplication>
        <delayDays>1</delayDays>
        <dismissButtonLabel>Dismiss</dismissButtonLabel>
        <displayPosition>TopCenter</displayPosition>
        <displayType>FloatingPanel</displayType>
        <experience>Lightning</experience>
        <isPublished>false</isPublished>
        <masterLabel>Activity Tab Step 1</masterLabel>
        <shouldDisplayActionButton>false</shouldDisplayActionButton>
        <shouldIgnoreGlobalDelay>false</shouldIgnoreGlobalDelay>
        <startDate>2026-09-11</startDate>
        <stepNumber>1</stepNumber>
        <targetPageKey1>home</targetPageKey1>
        <targetPageType>standard__namedPage</targetPageType>
        <themeColor>Theme1</themeColor>
        <themeSaturation>Dark</themeSaturation>
        <timesToDisplay>1</timesToDisplay>
        <title>Activities Tab Overview</title>
        <userAccess>Everyone</userAccess>
        <userProfileAccess>Everyone</userProfileAccess>
        <versionNumber>1</versionNumber>
    </promptVersions>
    <promptVersions>
        <body>&lt;p&gt;Click on&lt;strong&gt; More&lt;/strong&gt; from the menu bar and select &lt;strong&gt;Leads&lt;/strong&gt; from the drop-down menu to open the Leads workspace. Apart from Leads, the &lt;strong&gt;Activity&lt;/strong&gt; tab is also provided on Account, Contact and Opportunity records.&lt;/p&gt;</body>
        <customApplication>standard__LightningSales</customApplication>
        <dismissButtonLabel>Dismiss</dismissButtonLabel>
        <displayType>Targeted</displayType>
        <experience>Lightning</experience>
        <isPublished>false</isPublished>
        <masterLabel>Activity Tab Step 2</masterLabel>
        <referenceElementContext>{&quot;scope&quot;:{&quot;attributes&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;sfdc:TabDefinition.standard-Lead&quot;}},&quot;version&quot;:2}</referenceElementContext>
        <shouldDisplayActionButton>false</shouldDisplayActionButton>
        <shouldIgnoreGlobalDelay>false</shouldIgnoreGlobalDelay>
        <stepNumber>2</stepNumber>
        <targetPageKey1>home</targetPageKey1>
        <targetPageType>standard__namedPage</targetPageType>
        <title>Navigate to Leads</title>
        <userAccess>Everyone</userAccess>
        <userProfileAccess>Everyone</userProfileAccess>
        <versionNumber>1</versionNumber>
    </promptVersions>
    <promptVersions>
        <body>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Click on the Name&lt;/strong&gt; of the specific &lt;strong&gt;Lead&lt;/strong&gt; where you want to record the activity. This opens the Lead record, where you can access the &lt;strong&gt;Activity&lt;/strong&gt; tab to log Tasks, Calls, Events, and Emails.&lt;/p&gt;</body>
        <customApplication>standard__LightningSales</customApplication>
        <dismissButtonLabel>Dismiss</dismissButtonLabel>
        <displayPosition>BottomCenter</displayPosition>
        <displayType>FloatingPanel</displayType>
        <experience>Lightning</experience>
        <isPublished>false</isPublished>
        <masterLabel>Activity Tab Step 3</masterLabel>
        <shouldDisplayActionButton>false</shouldDisplayActionButton>
        <shouldIgnoreGlobalDelay>false</shouldIgnoreGlobalDelay>
        <stepNumber>3</stepNumber>
        <targetPageKey1>Lead</targetPageKey1>
        <targetPageKey2>list</targetPageKey2>
        <targetPageType>standard__objectPage</targetPageType>
        <title>Select the Lead</title>
        <userAccess>Everyone</userAccess>
        <userProfileAccess>Everyone</userProfileAccess>
        <versionNumber>1</versionNumber>
    </promptVersions>
    <promptVersions>
        <body>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Click on the Activity tab&lt;/strong&gt; to view and manage activities associated with the Lead. From here, you can create and track &lt;strong&gt;Tasks&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Calls&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Events&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;Emails&lt;/strong&gt; related to the record.&lt;/p&gt;</body>
        <customApplication>standard__LightningSales</customApplication>
        <dismissButtonLabel>Dismiss</dismissButtonLabel>
        <displayType>Targeted</displayType>
        <experience>Lightning</experience>
        <isPublished>false</isPublished>
        <masterLabel>Activity Tab Step 4</masterLabel>
        <referenceElementContext>{&quot;scope&quot;:{&quot;scope&quot;:{&quot;attributes&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;activityTabTab&quot;}},&quot;attributes&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;flexipage_tabset&quot;}},&quot;version&quot;:2}</referenceElementContext>
        <shouldDisplayActionButton>false</shouldDisplayActionButton>
        <shouldIgnoreGlobalDelay>false</shouldIgnoreGlobalDelay>
        <stepNumber>4</stepNumber>
        <targetPageKey1>Lead</targetPageKey1>
        <targetPageKey2>view</targetPageKey2>
        <targetPageType>standard__recordPage</targetPageType>
        <title>Navigate to Activity Tab</title>
        <userAccess>Everyone</userAccess>
        <userProfileAccess>Everyone</userProfileAccess>
        <versionNumber>1</versionNumber>
    </promptVersions>
    <promptVersions>
        <body>&lt;p&gt;Select &lt;strong&gt;New Task&lt;/strong&gt; to track customer commitments, follow-ups, action items and ARs. Tasks keep your to-do list organized in Sales CRM and can be linked to Accounts, Contacts, Leads, and Opportunities to improve productivity and deal management.&lt;/p&gt;</body>
        <customApplication>standard__LightningSales</customApplication>
        <dismissButtonLabel>Dismiss</dismissButtonLabel>
        <displayType>Targeted</displayType>
        <experience>Lightning</experience>
        <isPublished>false</isPublished>
        <masterLabel>Activity Tab Step 5</masterLabel>
        <referenceElementContext>{&quot;scope&quot;:{&quot;scope&quot;:{&quot;scope&quot;:{&quot;attributes&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;NewTaskTab&quot;}},&quot;attributes&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;runtime_sales_activities_activityPanel&quot;}},&quot;attributes&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;flexipage_tabset&quot;}},&quot;version&quot;:2,&quot;interactions&quot;:[{&quot;unless&quot;:{&quot;css&quot;:&quot;[aria-selected=true]&quot;},&quot;scope&quot;:{&quot;scope&quot;:{&quot;attributes&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;activityTabTab&quot;}},&quot;attributes&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;flexipage_tabset&quot;}},&quot;type&quot;:&quot;click&quot;}]}</referenceElementContext>
        <shouldDisplayActionButton>false</shouldDisplayActionButton>
        <shouldIgnoreGlobalDelay>false</shouldIgnoreGlobalDelay>
        <stepNumber>5</stepNumber>
        <targetPageKey1>Lead</targetPageKey1>
        <targetPageKey2>view</targetPageKey2>
        <targetPageType>standard__recordPage</targetPageType>
        <title>Create a New Task</title>
        <userAccess>Everyone</userAccess>
        <userProfileAccess>Everyone</userProfileAccess>
        <versionNumber>1</versionNumber>
    </promptVersions>
    <promptVersions>
        <body>&lt;p&gt;Select &lt;strong&gt;Log a Call&lt;/strong&gt; to capture customer conversations, meeting notes, outcomes, and next steps. Call details are saved as completed activities and linked to specific records, helping maintain an accurate history of customer interactions.&lt;/p&gt;</body>
        <customApplication>standard__LightningSales</customApplication>
        <dismissButtonLabel>Dismiss</dismissButtonLabel>
        <displayType>Targeted</displayType>
        <experience>Lightning</experience>
        <isPublished>false</isPublished>
        <masterLabel>Activity Tab Step 6</masterLabel>
        <referenceElementContext>{&quot;scope&quot;:{&quot;scope&quot;:{&quot;scope&quot;:{&quot;attributes&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;LogACallTab&quot;}},&quot;attributes&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;runtime_sales_activities_activityPanel&quot;}},&quot;attributes&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;flexipage_tabset&quot;}},&quot;version&quot;:2,&quot;interactions&quot;:[{&quot;unless&quot;:{&quot;css&quot;:&quot;[aria-selected=true]&quot;},&quot;scope&quot;:{&quot;scope&quot;:{&quot;attributes&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;activityTabTab&quot;}},&quot;attributes&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;flexipage_tabset&quot;}},&quot;type&quot;:&quot;click&quot;}]}</referenceElementContext>
        <shouldDisplayActionButton>false</shouldDisplayActionButton>
        <shouldIgnoreGlobalDelay>false</shouldIgnoreGlobalDelay>
        <stepNumber>6</stepNumber>
        <targetPageKey1>Lead</targetPageKey1>
        <targetPageKey2>view</targetPageKey2>
        <targetPageType>standard__recordPage</targetPageType>
        <title>Log a Call</title>
        <userAccess>Everyone</userAccess>
        <userProfileAccess>Everyone</userProfileAccess>
        <versionNumber>1</versionNumber>
    </promptVersions>
    <promptVersions>
        <body>&lt;p&gt;The New Event and Email options are available under the Activity tab of &lt;strong&gt;Opportunities&lt;/strong&gt;. Click New Event to log and track meetings. Click Email to send emails directly from Sales CRM, automatically linking communications to the opportunity record.&lt;/p&gt;</body>
        <customApplication>standard__LightningSales</customApplication>
        <dismissButtonLabel>Dismiss</dismissButtonLabel>
        <displayPosition>BottomCenter</displayPosition>
        <displayType>FloatingPanel</displayType>
        <experience>Lightning</experience>
        <isPublished>false</isPublished>
        <masterLabel>Activity Tab Step 7</masterLabel>
        <shouldDisplayActionButton>false</shouldDisplayActionButton>
        <shouldIgnoreGlobalDelay>false</shouldIgnoreGlobalDelay>
        <stepNumber>7</stepNumber>
        <targetPageKey1>Lead</targetPageKey1>
        <targetPageKey2>view</targetPageKey2>
        <targetPageType>standard__recordPage</targetPageType>
        <title>New Event and Email</title>
        <userAccess>Everyone</userAccess>
        <userProfileAccess>Everyone</userProfileAccess>
        <versionNumber>1</versionNumber>
    </promptVersions>
    <promptVersions>
        <body>&lt;p&gt;Add one or more contacts to a Task, Event, or Call during creation or through Edit. Open the activity record and click the pencil icon next to the Name field to add contacts. Once added, the activity appears in the contact&apos;s Activity timeline. &lt;/p&gt;</body>
        <customApplication>standard__LightningSales</customApplication>
        <dismissButtonLabel>Dismiss</dismissButtonLabel>
        <displayPosition>BottomCenter</displayPosition>
        <displayType>FloatingPanel</displayType>
        <experience>Lightning</experience>
        <isPublished>false</isPublished>
        <masterLabel>Activity Tab Step 8</masterLabel>
        <shouldDisplayActionButton>false</shouldDisplayActionButton>
        <shouldIgnoreGlobalDelay>false</shouldIgnoreGlobalDelay>
        <stepNumber>8</stepNumber>
        <targetPageKey1>Lead</targetPageKey1>
        <targetPageKey2>view</targetPageKey2>
        <targetPageType>standard__recordPage</targetPageType>
        <title>Associate a Contact with an Activity</title>
        <userAccess>Everyone</userAccess>
        <userProfileAccess>Everyone</userProfileAccess>
        <versionNumber>1</versionNumber>
    </promptVersions>
    <promptVersions>
        <body>&lt;p&gt;The&lt;strong&gt; Upcoming and Overdue&lt;/strong&gt; section helps you stay on track with activities and pending tasks. Select the checkbox to mark a task complete. Click the subject or action menu to view or edit details. Past activities are listed below, providing a timeline of completed interactions.&lt;/p&gt;</body>
        <customApplication>standard__LightningSales</customApplication>
        <dismissButtonLabel>Dismiss</dismissButtonLabel>
        <displayType>Targeted</displayType>
        <experience>Lightning</experience>
        <isPublished>false</isPublished>
        <masterLabel>Activity Tab Step 9</masterLabel>
        <referenceElementContext>{&quot;scope&quot;:{&quot;scope&quot;:{&quot;attributes&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;runtime_sales_activities_activityPanel&quot;}},&quot;attributes&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;flexipage_tabset&quot;}},&quot;version&quot;:2,&quot;interactions&quot;:[{&quot;unless&quot;:{&quot;css&quot;:&quot;[aria-selected=true]&quot;},&quot;scope&quot;:{&quot;scope&quot;:{&quot;attributes&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;activityTabTab&quot;}},&quot;attributes&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;flexipage_tabset&quot;}},&quot;type&quot;:&quot;click&quot;}]}</referenceElementContext>
        <shouldDisplayActionButton>false</shouldDisplayActionButton>
        <shouldIgnoreGlobalDelay>false</shouldIgnoreGlobalDelay>
        <stepNumber>9</stepNumber>
        <targetPageKey1>Lead</targetPageKey1>
        <targetPageKey2>view</targetPageKey2>
        <targetPageType>standard__recordPage</targetPageType>
        <title>Upcoming and Overdue</title>
        <userAccess>Everyone</userAccess>
        <userProfileAccess>Everyone</userProfileAccess>
        <versionNumber>1</versionNumber>
    </promptVersions>
    <promptVersions>
        <body>&lt;p&gt;You&apos;re now ready to use the &lt;strong&gt;Activity&lt;/strong&gt; tab to record tasks and customer interactions. Regularly logging activities helps maintain an accurate record of engagement history, improves team collaboration, and ensures important updates are easily accessible within Sales CRM.&lt;/p&gt;</body>
        <customApplication>standard__LightningSales</customApplication>
        <dismissButtonLabel>Dismiss</dismissButtonLabel>
        <displayPosition>BottomCenter</displayPosition>
        <displayType>FloatingPanel</displayType>
        <experience>Lightning</experience>
        <isPublished>false</isPublished>
        <masterLabel>Activity Tab Step 10</masterLabel>
        <shouldDisplayActionButton>false</shouldDisplayActionButton>
        <shouldIgnoreGlobalDelay>false</shouldIgnoreGlobalDelay>
        <stepNumber>10</stepNumber>
        <targetPageKey1>Lead</targetPageKey1>
        <targetPageKey2>view</targetPageKey2>
        <targetPageType>standard__recordPage</targetPageType>
        <title>Start Logging Activities</title>
        <userAccess>Everyone</userAccess>
        <userProfileAccess>Everyone</userProfileAccess>
        <versionNumber>1</versionNumber>
    </promptVersions>
</Prompt>
